        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01XAjJaYML4jrHgfKimwVxRJ",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: How credential-scoping and runtime-path decisions share a common architectural principle of centralizing configuration and security controls at startup.\\ntimestamp: 2025-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - pattern/SecurityByDesign\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both pages explicitly describe the same principle applied to different system concerns: centralized, validated startup configuration that prevents ambient mutation and scattering of logic across the codebase.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2026-01-14\\n---\\n\\n[[credential-scoping]] and [[runtime-paths]] are expressions of the same architectural\\nprinciple: **all critical system state \u2014 whether sensitive credentials or file locations\\n\u2014 is composed, validated, and distributed at a single point during startup**, never\\ndiscovered, mutated, or scattered across the codebase at runtime.\\n\\n**Credential-scoping** centralizes credential injection: the Hub never holds the\\nAnthropic API key in its own process environment. Instead, a secrets loader reads from\\nconfiguration exactly once at startup and injects it only into the child process that\\nneeds it (Ingest or Query agent), immediately before that process starts. No other\\npart of the system can inadvertently leak or misuse the credential by inspecting the\\nHub\u0027s own environment.\\n\\n**Runtime-paths** centralizes path resolution: the Hub resolves every file-system\\nlocation in exactly one place at startup \u2014 a single path resolver reads configuration,\\nvalidates every required input exists, auto-creates missing directories, and reports\\nthe effective value. No other part of the codebase is allowed to rediscover locations\\non its own; everything downstream consumes the already-resolved path set instead.\\n\\nBoth patterns prevent the same classes of failure:\\n- **Ambient discovery**: neither credentials nor paths are left to be rediscovered on\\n  demand, where they might be found in the wrong place or with incorrect validation.\\n- **Scattered logic**: security and configuration concerns are not duplicated across\\n  multiple modules; they live in one place, where they can be audited, tested, and\\n  evolved together.\\n- **Runtime mutation**: credentials are not inherited from parent processes and paths\\n  are not modified after initial validation; the composition is fixed and immutable\\n  for the lifetime of the process.\\n\\nAdding a new credential (e.g., a different API key for a different vendor) or a new\\nruntime location (e.g., a new agent\u0027s instruction directory) both follow the same\\npattern: extend the one composition point, not scatter the change across the codebase.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
